  "query_preview": "..issued at 3 am.\nSevere and flash flooding risk will be the main focus today as \nthe strong upper level low approaching srn CA this morning moves\ninland and then lifts to the NE as the day progresses. PWATs \nremain elevated across the area, running 250-280% of normal for \nlate October. Any thunderstorm today, especially N-NE of Tucson,\nwill be capable of severe wind gusts of 58 mph or greater \n(15-18% chance), large hail of 1\" or greater (15-17% chance), a \ntornado (5-8% chance of one occurring within 25 miles of a \npoint), and rainfall rates of 1-2\"/hr. SPC severe weather \noutlook has eastern Pinal/Pima, nrn Cochise, and all of Graham \nand Greenlee counties with Slight Risk. WPC has the area \nnortheast of a Florence-Oracle-Willcox- San Simon line with \nSlight Risk of flash flooding. Current Flash flood watch remains\nin effect today for Pinal, Graham and Greenlee counties. CWA in\na Marginal with a Slight from Tucson NE. Once again, \n\nDrier air moves in for Friday, though some lingering showers \npossible near the NM border, which could linger into the weekend\nas well. \n\nTemperatures near normal today, then cooler than normal Friday \ninto this weekend. Latest NBM has a freeze potential at the \nhighest elevations of the White Mountains Sun/Mon morning.",
